 The doors needs:    AEDoor.Library in your LIBS:  (made by Sintax/WoT)
                     Restrict.info in Doors:Restrict/
                     ToolTypes explained below
 
 It's XIM - Fast assembler :)


WhAt'S rEsTrIct ?
-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-

 >Refer< is basically a door to kick users from the board by dropping
a carrier. It can be *very* useful under certain circumstances :-)
You can for example prevent sysop logins on modem nodes and prevent
hacking with your handle, you can restrict some users to call only at
certain hourz, select the user you wish but also kick everybody with
"*" as name. Useful when you decide to close the board for a while. You just
use the door and nobody is allowed to call, except your friends if
you wish.


'bOuT tHe ToOlTyPeS & iNsTaLlAtIoN
*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-

 Make a directory RESTRICT in your DOORS:  drawer (must be assigned) and copy
the door in it + its icon. Put in your BBS:Commands/BBSCmd drawer the door
icon like for all doors. And again... if you don't have the AEDoor.Library
by Sintax/WoT installed, don't expect the door to work !

 Sysops using /X v1.x -> 2.x will know better than me how to configurate
the whole thing. The only thing which changes is the door def. wich
corresponds to the icon located in Commands/BBSCmd (stack, type, location,
etc...)

The tooltypes are:

 NAME.x= ***             Users to be kicked
                          eg: Name.1=Diogenes
 
 PASSWORD.x= ***         This will cause the door to ask the user for
                         a password. In case of password failure, the door
                         will start the drop carrier procedure. Else the
                         user will be allowed to log in. This can be used
                         for the sysop to have a second password check,
                         so he still can call his board from elsewhere.

 TEXT.x= ***             Here you type the string to send to the user
                         before kicking him
                                               OR
                         a PATH to a text file. If TEXT.x doesn't exist,
                         the default string will be "ACCESS DENIED".
 
 FLAG.x= Path/Line       If you chose a path to a text file for TEXT.x,
                         state here PATH. If not, TEXT.x will be considered
                         as a simple string.
 
 TIME.x= 0000,2359       States the interval of time when the user MAY
                         call. Outside, he will be kicked.
                         It MUST be 4 digits long. A coma is needed between
                         both hourz. The first is the earliest time allowed
                         and the other the latest.
                         eg: 1000,1700 means that the user may call between
                             10.00 am and 05.00 pm (or 17.00).
                         
                         Only this format is allowed. And of course,
                         above 2359 is forbidden too.
                         
                         0000 stands for midnight, beginning of the day.
                         2359 is the end of the day.
                         
                         This is useful to prevent real leechers from
                         calling when uploaders try to come.


 The little "x" stands for a number from 1 to 4.294.967.295. Enough ? ;-)

 Examples:
 --------
 
 1] Name.1=Diogenes            Only Diogenes is kicked. Default string is
                               used (ACCESS DENIED)
 
 2] Name.1=Diogenes
    Time.1=0000,2359
    Name.2=*                   Diogenes may call all the day. All the other
                               users will be kicked.
                               Yeh, you can also specify users NOT to be
                               kicked this way ;-)

 3] Name.1=Diogenes            Sysop Diogenes can log in IF he knows the
    Password.1=Zoup            password.

 4] Name.1=Diogenes
    Text.1=BBS:Screens/Node1/Bye.Txt
    Flag.1=Path
    Name.2=Bip
    Text.2=Bye bye !           Guess what ;-)
    
 
 For those who wonder how to call the door, here's where I call it:
 BULLxx.TXT in my BBS:Screens/Nodex drawer.  The BULL.TXT of the local
 node shouldn't call the door as one of the main purposes is to prevent
 sysop logins and leechers from calling at the busiest hourz. The sysop must
 still be able to enter his local node ;-)
 


